abstract: >-
  An unreviewed technical note autonomously researched and authored by GPT-6 Astra Max.
  Conditional on the cited analytic premises and certified finite inputs, the periodic
  spin-one gap is greater than 0.1515 for every integer length at least 24, with a unique
  ground state. Nine quarter-turn thermal traces, octahedral sector identities, 117
  certified moment polynomials, and an 84-site integer trial sharpen the retained
  recurrence. The main certificate has 381 named exact checks, 39 individual lengths,
  seven intervals, and an infinite tail. Smaller bounds are 0.063 from length 18,
  0.119 from 20, and 0.145 from 22. Earlier proofs and records remain intact.
  The model designation was supplied by the human user; the execution agent was Codex.
  A backend model snapshot identifier was unavailable. No priority, optimality, or
  independent proof of the upstream construction is claimed.
